    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Neotsu is an unincorporated community in Lincoln County situated on the northern shore of Devils Lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neotsu%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Neotsu is located exactly on the 45th parallel north.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neotsu%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Neotsu was formally established in 1900 when it received a post office during a period of pioneer development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/neotsu_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The name Neotsu is said to be a Native American word meaning lake near the ocean.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/neotsu_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Local Indigenous legends once associated the nearby lake with malevolent spirits known as skookums.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/neotsu_oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The region around Neotsu was part of the traditional territory of the Salish-speaking Tillamook people.",
